>If they found it tricky to remember, try doing three different actions.</li>\n<li>When they get really good at remembering three actions, try increasing the challenge by having four words. How many words can you get up to? </li>\n<li>Repeat the activity with your child saying the actions and you trying to remember!</li>\n</ol>\n", "modal": {"steps": [null], "details": null}, "order": 3, "btnType": null, "linkUrl": null, "audioUrl": null, "fileName": null, "fontSize": null, "fontType": null, "imageUrl": null, "linkName": null, "stepType": "TEXT_AND_IMAGE", "tabsData": null, "deletedAt": null, "tableData": null, "timerData": null, "activityId": 2950, "dimensions": null, "editAsHtml": false, "properties": null, "deletedById": null, "downloadUrl": null, "editorState": null, "carouselData": null, "downloadName": null, "accordionData": null, "includeSeconds": null, "selectedModalId": null, "textCarouselData": null, "checkListTextData": null, "imageCarouselData": null, "checklistImageData": null, "clickableAlphabetData": null}]